        "modelStatedGap": ", but the marketing is stronger than the proof**.\n\n## Bottom line\nThe Stem Company’s ReGenerative Serum is probably best viewed as a **premium “bioactive / growth-factor-style” serum**, not a miracle anti-aging treatment. It may help with:\n\n- hydration\n- glow\n- barrier support\n- mild texture improvement\n- maybe some fine-line softening over time\n\nBut I would **not** assume it can outperform the best-proven anti-aging staples like:\n\n- ** sunscreen**\n- **retinoids**\n- **vitamin C**\n- **niacinamide / peptides** in well-formulated products\n\n---\n\n## What their science claims seem to mean\nFrom the science page you shared, they say:\n\n- the product does **not contain human stem cells**\n- it uses **plant stem cells and proprietary process to create“Consortia Factors™”**\n- those factors supposedly include **peptides, exosomes, and rejuvenating bioactives**\n- they frame it ascell-to-bottle” and “skin speaking its language”\n\nThat language is very marketable, but scientifically it raises a few questions:\n\n1. **What exactly are the ingredients?**  \n   “Consortia Factors” is proprietary, so you’re getting full transparency.\n\n2. **Are independent clinical trials**  \n   I’d want to see, controlled human studies on the actual serum, not just on similar ingredient classes.\n\n3. **Areexosomes” in there, from what source?**  \n   Exosome claims in cosmetics are vague, branded, and not always easy to## What evidence\nThe broader science ** stem extracts,-factor ingredients and ferment bio** is but not nonsense.\n\n### What may be real\n- Some in category can improve **hydr- Some may help with **skin barrier repair**\n may have **ioxidant** orsoothing**\n- Certain-factor-style can showmod** improvement in/ in studies\n\n### What not well established\n- productsfully “regenerate” skin in a dramatic way\n- that theyino, lasers or treatments- that brand-specific proprietary consistently outperform simpler evidence-based formulas---\n\n How judge this serum realistically\n you’re considering buying it, a..."
